2. If you pushed numbers onto a stack in the following order: 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6,
and then popped two items, which number would you be able to read
from the stack?

answer:
ok so lets say at first we have an empty stack
heres the thing we wanna push lets say xs = '(1 2 3 4 5 6)

we push them in order so in the stack we have
stack = '(6 5 4 3 2 1)

then we pop the two items so now the stack is
stack = '(4 3 2 1)

and now we perform read which basically reads the top of the stack (car stack)
which outputs 4

